# TripleUCrypt — Environment Configuration
#
# Copy to .env  (cp .env.example .env)  and fill in your credentials.
#
# You do NOT need this file to trade. There are THREE signers (market data +
# charts always work with NO credentials):
#   • BROWSER WALLET (no .env at all): switch signing to "Browser (wallet)" in
#     the Wallet panel and let MetaMask sign. No key ever reaches this app.
#     Recommended if you're running this repo for the first time.
#   • GENERATED WALLET (no .env):  leave the two POLY_* vars unset and click
#     "Generate trading wallet" in the app — it creates + stores a dedicated key
#     locally and signs server-side. The right choice for a headless/VPS box.
#   • EXISTING KEY (this file):    paste a Polymarket account key below.
# With none of the three set up, the app stays in practice (paper) mode.
#
# Security: any key here lives only in .env, which is git-ignored and never
# committed. The app passes it solely to @polymarket/clob-client-v2 against clob.polymarket.com.

# ══ OPTION 1 — existing Polymarket account (optional) ═════════════════════════
# If set, these take PRECEDENCE over a generated wallet (existing setups are
# unchanged). Leave them unset/placeholder to use Option 2 instead.
# Your Ethereum (Polygon) private key. Funds and signs the trades. KEEP SECRET.
POLY_PRIVATE_KEY=0x_your_ethereum_private_key_here
# The Polymarket-funded (proxy) wallet address that holds your USDC.
POLY_WALLET_ADDRESS=0x_your_polymarket_wallet_address_here

# ══ OPTION 2 — generated local trading wallet (no key to paste) ═══════════════
# Leave the two POLY_* vars above unset and the app generates a dedicated trading
# wallet, stored under $TC_DATA_DIR (default ~/.triplecrypt) as trading_wallet.json
# (locked 0600) — or an encrypted keystore if you generate it with a password.
# Fund the address shown in the Wallet panel with USDC on Polygon, plus a little
# POL for the one-time on-chain trading approval (a raw wallet pays its own gas).
#
# Real-money on-chain ops (approve / withdraw / redeem) no longer need an .env
# flag — they unlock at runtime when you click "Enable trading" in the Wallet
# panel and accept the confirm dialog (per-process; resets on restart). The
# legacy flags below still work for headless/automated setups if you prefer them.
#TUC_EOA_APPROVE_ENABLED=0
#TUC_REDEEM_ENABLED=0
# Swap card / "Get gas" — both broadcast real on-chain txs (Uniswap V3 trade,
# USDC→POL gas top-up), so they are default-OFF too. Armed by the same in-app
# "Enable trading" confirm, or set this for headless/automated setups.
#TUC_SWAP_ENABLED=0
# Only if you chose the ENCRYPTED option, set the password so the backend can
# unlock the key to sign at startup:
#TUC_WALLET_PASSWORD=your_keystore_password

# ══ OPTIONAL ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Polymarket CLOB API credentials (L2) — LEGACY / UNUSED ───────────────────
# The app derives the L2 API creds from POLY_PRIVATE_KEY at runtime (the
# canonical Polymarket flow), so these are NOT read; any stored ones are
# ignored. Kept here only for compatibility with older setups.
#POLY_API_KEY=your_polymarket_api_key_here
#POLY_API_SECRET=your_polymarket_api_secret_here
#POLY_API_PASSPHRASE=your_polymarket_api_passphrase_here

# ── Polygon RPC endpoint (balance reads) ─────────────────────────────────────
# Defaults to the public https://polygon-rpc.com — set your own (Alchemy,
# Infura, …) if the public one rate-limits you.
#POLYGON_RPC=https://polygon-rpc.com

# ── Deposit/transfer history (wallet panel) ──────────────────────────────────
# Etherscan V2 API key for the token-transfer history. NOTE: the endpoint is
# Etherscan V2 — you need an etherscan.io API key, NOT a legacy polygonscan.com
# key. Without it, deposit history is simply hidden.
#POLYGONSCAN_API_KEY=your_etherscan_v2_api_key_here

# ── In-app swap + auto-gas (Swap card / "Get gas") ───────────────────────────
# Swaps (native USDC ↔ USDC.e, USDC → POL gas) go straight through Uniswap V3
# on-chain — no API key needed. Optionally tune the gas floor the wallet keeps
# before auto-topping-up (default 0.05 POL).
#TUC_MIN_GAS_POL=0.05

# ── Send / withdraw (Phase 2 — gated, off by default) ────────────────────────
# Set to 1/true to enable the on-chain send feature. Requires the BUILDER_*
# relayer creds below. Leave unset to keep send disabled (preview only).
#TUC_SEND_ENABLED=0
# Polymarket relayer (builder) API credentials — used ONLY for gasless sends
# from the funder proxy. These are different from the CLOB L2 creds above.
#BUILDER_API_KEY=
#BUILDER_API_SECRET=
#BUILDER_API_PASSPHRASE=

# ── Deployment / storage ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public HTTPS URL when serving behind a domain (baked into the frontend at
# build/export time — see DEPLOY.md). Leave unset for local use.
#TUC_API_URL=https://trade.example.com
# Where the practice-mode (paper) ledger persists. Defaults to ~/.triplecrypt.
# In Docker, set it to /app/data — that path is the compose-persisted volume.
#TC_DATA_DIR=/app/data
